Package: descriptiveStats
Type: Package
Title: Descriptive Statistics for Numeric Vectors and Data Frames
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Eniola", "Ajayi", email = "eniolaajayi.py@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements common descriptive statistics from first principles:
    arithmetic mean, median, mode, first and third quartiles and the
    interquartile range. Every function validates its input, handles missing
    values, empty vectors and single values consistently, and gives
    informative error messages. Quartiles support the Hyndman and Fan (1996)
    sample quantile definitions used by default in R (type 7), SAS (type 2)
    and SPSS/Minitab (type 6). describe_stats() applies all of them to the
    numeric columns of a data frame, overall or by group, like PROC MEANS
    with a CLASS statement in SAS.
